Auto-clear is best done right before you log the new start time, so every run starts clean and you never mix old data with a new run.

Below are two safe ways. Pick what fits your flow.


---

✅ Option 1: Auto-clear Start / End / Duration at Macro Start (Recommended)

Clear before logging the new start time.

🔹 Update your Main Macro

Sub RunMainProcess()

    ' Clear previous run
    Call ClearTimeLog

    ' Log start time
    Call LogStartTime

    ' ===== YOUR MAIN CODE GOES HERE =====
    Application.Wait Now + TimeValue("00:00:05")
    ' ===================================

    ' Log end time and duration
    Call LogEndTimeAndDuration

End Sub


---

🔹 Clear Sub (Auto-Reset)

Sub ClearTimeLog()

    With ThisWorkbook.Sheets("Summary") ' change sheet name
        .Range("A2:A4").ClearContents
    End With

End Sub

📌 What this clears

A2 → Start Date & Time

A3 → End Date & Time

A4 → Duration



---

✅ Option 2: Clear Only End Time & Duration (Keeps Last Start)

Use this if you want the start time overwritten, but still reset old end/duration values.

Sub ClearEndTimeOnly()

    With ThisWorkbook.Sheets("Summary")
        .Range("A3:A4").ClearContents
    End With

End Sub

Call it before LogStartTime.


---

🧠 Best Practice Tip

To avoid accidental clearing while debugging:

If MsgBox("Start new run and clear previous time log?", _
          vbYesNo + vbQuestion) = vbYes Then
    Call ClearTimeLog
End If

